    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a volatile slate today, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** serving as our clear primary anchor. He enters the matchup against Legumina with a score of 70.14, buoyed by an opportunistic pairing of a favorable 4.32 xERA opposing starter and a premier #2 spot in the order. While the dynamic platoon disadvantage against a right-hander pulls his floor back slightly, his recent form and park factors keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" category. Behind him, **Drake Baldwin** holds onto the second spot in our daily priorities with a 59.84, pushed to the brink of elite status by his leadoff assignment against Hart; the 3.98 xERA of the opposing starter is manageable, and his impressive 0.387 xwOBA suggests he is primed to capitalize on the early-game volume.\n\nLower in the priority list, we are forced to navigate thin margins. **Brayan Rocchio** occupies the 2B slot with a 46.89 score, hampered by Bradley\u2019s solid 3.82 xERA and a standard platoon disadvantage, making him a marginal play today. **Dominic Smith** is our most vulnerable starter at 40.47; he is actively fading due to the L/L matchup against Hart and a suboptimal #7 spot in the order. While he remains in the lineup to maximize our daily plate appearance caps, he sits on the razor's edge of being benched. The \"most interesting bench decision\" is effectively moot today, as core producers like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** are unavailable due to team off-days. With **Andy Pages** and others also sidelined, the optimizer\u2019s lack of depth forces a \"start what you have\" approach rather than a competitive selection process. Monitor the weather in these venues, as any late-breaking precipitation could jeopardize the viability of **Dominic Smith** and **Brayan Rocchio**, whose marginal scores do not afford us the luxury of high-variance, rain-shortened outcomes.",
